{
  "_doc": "Cinematic capture shot list (fx test source set only, never ships). Shots named in 'run' are rendered by the fx client gametest (tools/gpu-test.sh fx) instead of the normal fx tests; leave 'run' empty for normal tests. Modes: free (keys = camera), follow (keys = vehicle route, camera behind), cockpit (keys = aircraft route, camera in the seat), boat (keys = boat route on the water, camera behind). Key fields: t (s), pos [x,y,z] (y above ground when relativeY) or site + uv [u along the landmark, v out of its front; negative v = street/ocean side for Ocean Drive hotels L25-L51] + y, yaw, pitch, fov (whole degrees: vanilla's FOV option is an integer, so animate it only in big moves). time = day time ticks (6000 noon, 11800 golden hour, 18000 night). snapToRoad: move key x to the centre of the nearest road. brightness: game brightness 0..1 (vanilla gamma option). dhRendering (top level, default true): Distant Horizons LODs on for the capture. exposure: post exposure in stops applied at encode (e.g. 0.7 for night). Extra key fields: view 'vc:<site>:<view>' or 'lm:<site>:<view>' (landmark camera preset; offset/lookOffset world deltas), look [x,y,z] (aim; y above ground when relativeY), lookUv [u,h,v] with site, absY true (key y absolute even when relativeY). preview (top level): render 3 quick stills per shot (10/50/90 %), no encode. Pop-in rules: every shot gets a warm-up flight along its path and a per-frame terrain gate (Sodium terrain complete, 2 s cap, capped frames logged); renderDistance 32 by default so DH only shows beyond loaded chunks. Mode thirdperson: the player (character jason|lucia, HD model) walks the key path with vanilla third-person camera at cameraDistance (3.5 on foot) and key pitch; with entity the player rides and drives that vehicle along the path (cameraDistance 6).",
